1
00:03:28,421 --> 00:03:34,421
Celebrate 30 years of The King of Pop!

2
00:06:56,842 --> 00:07:02,842
Michael Jackson: 30th Anniversary Celebration is a music,
documentary film directed by Bruce Gowers.

3
00:10:25,263 --> 00:10:31,263
The Michael Jackson: 30th Anniversary Special was a 2001
New York City revue show by Michael Jackson.

4
00:13:53,684 --> 00:13:59,684
It took place on September 7, 2001 and September 10, 2001.

5
00:17:22,105 --> 00:17:28,105
In late November 2001, the CBS television network aired the concerts as a two-hour special in honour of Michael Jackson's
thirtieth year as a solo entertainer (his first solo single, "Got to Be There", was recorded in 1971).

6
00:20:50,526 --> 00:20:56,526
The show was edited from footage of two separate concerts Michael had orchestrated in New
York City's Madison Square Garden on September 7 and September 10 of 2001.

7
00:24:18,947 --> 00:24:24,947
The shows sold out in five hours.

8
00:27:47,368 --> 00:27:53,368
Ticket prices were pop's most expensive ever; the best seats cost $5,000 and
included a dinner with Michael Jackson and a signed poster.

9
00:31:15,789 --> 00:31:21,789
Self, played by Michael Jackson.

10
00:34:44,210 --> 00:34:50,210
Self, played by Muhammad Ali.

11
00:38:12,631 --> 00:38:18,631
Self, played by Marc Anthony.

12
00:41:41,052 --> 00:41:47,052
Self, played by Monica.

13
00:45:09,473 --> 00:45:15,473
Self, played by Marlon Brando.

14
00:48:37,894 --> 00:48:43,894
Self, played by Cyd Charisse.

15
00:52:06,315 --> 00:52:12,315
Michael Joseph Jackson (August 29, 1958 – June 25, 2009) was an
American singer, songwriter, dancer, and philanthropist.

16
00:55:34,736 --> 00:55:40,736
Dubbed the "King of Pop", he is widely regarded as one of the most
culturally significant figures of the 20th century.

17
00:59:03,157 --> 00:59:09,157
Over a four-decade career, his musical achievements broke American
racial barriers and made him a dominant figure worldwide.

18
01:02:31,578 --> 01:02:37,578
Through his songs, concerts, and fashion, he proliferated visual performance for artists in popular music,
popularizing street dance moves such as the moonwalk, the robot, and the anti-gravity lean.

19
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Jackson is often deemed the greatest entertainer of all time.

20
01:09:28,421 --> 01:09:34,421
The eighth child of the Jackson family, Michael made his public debut at age six as
the lead singer of the Jackson 5, one of Motown's most successful acts.

21
01:12:56,842 --> 01:13:02,842
He rose to solo stardom with the album Off the Wall (1979) and achieved unprecedented
global success with Thriller (1982), the best-selling album in history.

22
01:16:25,263 --> 01:16:31,263
Its short film-style music videos for "Thriller", "Beat It", and
"Billie Jean" redefined the medium as an art form.

23
01:19:53,684 --> 01:19:59,684
Jackson followed it with Bad (1987), the first album to produce five US Billboard Hot 100 number-one singles: "I Just
Can't Stop Loving You", "Bad", "The Way You Make Me Feel", "Man in the Mirror", and "Dirty Diana".

24
01:23:22,105 --> 01:23:28,105
His next two albums, Dangerous (1991) and HIStory (1995), explored socially
conscious themes while Invincible (2001) delved into more personal topics.

25
01:26:50,526 --> 01:26:56,526
From the mid-1980s, Jackson came under public scrutiny due to changes in
his appearance, relationships, behavior, and lifestyle.

26
01:30:18,947 --> 01:30:24,947
He was accused of sexually abusing the child of a family friend in 1993.

27
01:33:47,368 --> 01:33:53,368
In 2005, Jackson was tried and acquitted of further
such allegations and other charges.

28
01:37:15,789 --> 01:37:21,789
In 2009, while preparing for This Is It, a series of comeback concerts, he died from an overdose of propofol
administered by his personal physician Conrad Murray, who was convicted of involuntary manslaughter in 2011.

29
01:40:44,210 --> 01:40:50,210
Jackson's death triggered global reactions, creating unprecedented
surges of internet traffic and a spike in his music sales.

30
01:44:12,631 --> 01:44:18,631
His televised memorial service, held at the Staples Center in Los Angeles, is
estimated to have been viewed by more than 2.5 billion people.

31
01:47:41,052 --> 01:47:47,052
Jackson is one of the best-selling music artists of all time,
with estimated sales of over 500 million records.

32
01:51:09,473 --> 01:51:15,473
He holds a joint-record for a male solo artist with 13 Billboard Hot 100 number-one
singles and is the only artist to have a top-ten single in six decades.

33
01:54:37,894 --> 01:54:43,894
One of the most-awarded music artists in history, Jackson received 13 Grammy Awards, the Grammy Legend Award, and the Grammy Lifetime Achievement
Award; 26 American Music Awards; 12 World Music Awards; eight MTV Video Music Awards; six Brit Awards; and three presidential honors.

34
01:58:06,315 --> 01:58:12,315
He was inducted into numerous halls of fame, including the Rock and Roll Hall of
Fame twice, the Songwriters Hall of Fame, and the Dance Hall of Fame.

35
02:01:34,736 --> 02:01:40,736
Having donated an estimated $500 million, Jackson is credited
with setting a standard for celebrity charity.

36
02:05:03,157 --> 02:05:09,157
In 2024, half of his music catalogue was sold to Sony for $600
million, the largest music acquisition for a single artist.

37
02:08:31,578 --> 02:08:37,578
The film explores themes of concert, pop, rock
music, live performance, pop music.
